# docs/plans 于 2026-10-07 起纳入版本管理（计划与备忘历史恢复）；
# 仅继续忽略 Windows ADS 残留 junk
*:Zone.Identifier
references/
.worktrees/
.pnpm-store/

# test infrastructure (test-infra-standardization, 2026-09-12):
# pristine upstream DSH checkout used as the test runtime (its own git repo;
# never committed — see docs/TEST_METHODS.md). The frozen legacy reference
# stays under references/ (read-only).
tests/deepseek-harness-test-use/
# per-world DSH_HOME dirs (world state, launch tokens — never committed;
# naming + cleanup protocol in docs/TEST_METHODS.md §7)
tests/homes/
# user-directed DSH_HOME base dir for test runs (archive-member round +
# PR #26 supplemental git-install boot probe, 2026-09-21) — same
# never-committed discipline as tests/homes/
tests/dsh-homes/
# real published-host npm install for the alpha.2 0.1.5-rc.2 live smoke
# (task fix/alpha2-explicit-agent-setup-compat; npm node_modules — never
# committed; reinstall: npm install --no-save @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2
# in that directory)
tests/live-host-015rc2/

# build & tooling (P1-T4 skeleton)
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# client composition shim (generated by pnpm build:composition; R125)
packages/client/composition-shim/

# Shipped prebuilt install-surface artifacts (plugin-prebuilt-artifacts, R131):
# these two paths ARE the plugin's git-install surface (root `files` whitelist)
# and are committed prebuilt so `pnpm dsh plugin add github:...` executes NO build
# scripts (no pnpm `allowBuilds` entry needed). All other dist/ dirs stay ignored.
# Discipline: source changes affecting these artifacts must commit the rebuilt
# artifacts in the same commit — `pnpm build:composition` runs the freshness gate
# (scripts/check-artifacts-committed.mjs) and fails otherwise.
!packages/runtime/dist/
!packages/client/composition-shim/

# characterization harness per-run scratch (P2 integration)
tests/characterization/.run-logs/

# test scratch (runtime artifacts from .test.ts worlds; the test pre-clean
# destroyDir already handles staleness on every run)
packages/testkit/test/.tmp-fault/
# Scratch HOME worlds must never be tracked: the documented "clear the scratch
# residue" remedy (dev/agent-workflow evidence, .tmp-fault flake class) deletes
# them, and a tracked file inside one turns that cleanup into a working-tree
# deletion. Untracked here on the A4-PR7 lane (2026-10-07, coordinator instruction).
.tmp-*-home/

# 0.2.0-rc.2 upgrade round: kit/probe scratch worlds + private raw evidence
# (raw host logs are kept byte-identically here, NEVER committed; committed
# copies are the sanitized ones — see evidence/dsh-020rc2-upgrade/SANITIZATION.json)
.private-raw-evidence/
.sanitized-tmp/
.tmp-npmcache/
.*-blueprints-*/

.tmp-faultscratch/

# Raw vitest JSON run reports stay out of git (multi-MB each); the record is the
# normalized identity list + human-readable logs. Regenerate only if a receipt is needed.
dev/agent-workflow/evidence/**/root-vitest*.json

# V8 isolate / crash dumps are multi-MB and never a record
*.log.isolate
isolate-*.log

# local scratch / caches (coordinator + worker), never committable — SESSION_ROUTER_LOG 2026-10-07
# every PR gate asserts "tree clean after build"; 14 untracked-AND-unignored entries (incl. a 650 MB
# store) made that signal unreachable, and this repo already had a git add -A accident (log 2026-10-07).
# NOTE: packages/*/dist stays tracked on purpose (plan rule 8) — do not ignore it.
.tmp-xdg/
.tmp-pnpm-store/
.tmp-npm-cache/
.tmp-superpowers/
.tmp-spill-compare/
.tmp-scratch-backup-*/
.tmp-local-evidence-backup/
.pnpm-store-testuse/
.dsh-vision-toolkit/
.worktrees/
*.tgz
spike-run*.log
.tmp-resolve-probe.mjs
agent-sandbox-hotfix-*.sh
